From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 11:41:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa: don't starve non-command channels with a WRR weight
 of 0

gsi_channel_program() programs the channel QOS register and leaves
WRR_WEIGHT at 0 for every channel that is not the AP command channel.
On IPA v3.1 (msm8998) a weight of 0 means the channel gets no share of
GSI's weighted round-robin scheduler at all: the modem TX channel moves
exactly one TRE off the doorbell written at channel start and is then
never scheduled again.

The failure is silent and does not look like a scheduling problem:

  - the channel sits in STARTED with a valid doorbell, but its read
    pointer stops one TRE in (ch_hw=1 while the doorbell is at 3)
  - with no TX completions, IPA calls netdev_sent_queue() but never
    netdev_completed_queue(), so BQL's inflight only grows
  - once inflight passes the limit the stack sets
    __QUEUE_STATE_STACK_XOFF, the qdisc stops dequeuing and
    ipa_start_xmit() is never called again, so the driver logs nothing
  - IPA defines no .ndo_tx_timeout, so dev_watchdog() is never armed
    and nothing warns

The result is a permanent, silent stall: the un-XOFF only happens inside
netdev_tx_completed_queue(), which needs a completion that can never
arrive.

Downstream never programs 0. ipa_v3/ipa_dp.c uses the maximum weight for
IPA_CLIENT_APPS_CMD_PROD and 1 for every other channel.

Give non-command channels a weight of 1 to match. With this, mobile data
works: the TX ring drains, BQL returns to inflight 0, and the GSI
interrupt count climbs instead of being frozen.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/net/ipa/gsi.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ipa/gsi.c b/drivers/net/ipa/gsi.c
index 4c3227e77898..0cb7649b972e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ipa/gsi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa/gsi.c
@@ -866,6 +866,8 @@ static void gsi_channel_program(struct gsi_channel *channel, bool doorbell)
 	/* Command channel gets low weighted round-robin priority */
 	if (channel->command)
 		wrr_weight = reg_field_max(reg, WRR_WEIGHT);
+	else
+		wrr_weight = 1;		/* never 0: 0 starves the channel */
 	val = reg_encode(reg, WRR_WEIGHT, wrr_weight);
 
 	/* Max prefetch is 1 segment (do not set MAX_PREFETCH_FMASK) */
